      ":question/problem": "Consider the matrix $M,$ given by\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 2 & 4 \\\\ 8 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -1 & 9\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWhat matrix results from carrying out the row operation ${R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+3{R}_{1}$ on $M?$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The operation ${R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+3{R}_{1}$ means that we need to add $3$ times the first row to the third row.\n\nApplying this row operation, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 2 & 4 \\\\ 8 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -1 & 9\\end{bmatrix}\\,{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & \\sim{\\small \\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 2 & 4 \\\\ 8 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 3+(3)(-1) & -1+(3)(2) & 9+(3)(4)\\end{bmatrix}} \\\\  & \\sim\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 2 & 4 \\\\ 8 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 21\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
