      ":question/id": "321745fd-75bf-57ae-b27b-649a283a9df9",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the matrix $C,$ given by\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 4 & 7 \\\\ 5 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWhat matrix results from carrying out the following row operations on $C?$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}-2{R}_{2} \\\\ {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+{R}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Let's list the required operations:\n\n- The operation ${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}-2{R}_{2}$ means that we need to add $-2$ times the second row to the first row.\n\n- The operation ${R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+{R}_{2}$ means that we need to add $1$ times the second row to the third row.\n\nApplying the operations, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}C & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 4 & 7 \\\\ 5 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\quad {R}_{1}:={R}_{1}-2{R}_{2} \\\\  & \\sim \\begin{bmatrix}0+(-2)(5) & 4+(-2)(2) & 7+(-2)(1) \\\\ 5 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & \\sim \\begin{bmatrix}-10 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 5 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\quad {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+{R}_{2} \\\\  & \\sim \\begin{bmatrix}-10 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 5 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 1+(1)(5) & 3+(1)(2) & 0+(1)(1)\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & \\sim \\begin{bmatrix}-10 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 5 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 6 & 5 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
